==============================================================================
PART B: pinning down kappa_0(gamma), the EXACT wave-17 truncation constant
==============================================================================

Wave-17 front's own truncation (gamma_scaling_attempt/ATTEMPT.md Section 5, quoted verbatim):
  K := ceil( sqrt( (4/beta) * n * ln(n) ) ),  beta := gamma*(2-gamma)/2

Hence K^2 = (4/beta) n ln n + O(sqrt(n ln n))  (ceiling correction),
i.e. in the Gap-1 front's own notation 'K^2 = kappa_0 * n * ln n':

  kappa_0(gamma) = 4/beta = -8/(gamma*(gamma - 2))

kappa_0(gamma=1)      = 8
kappa_0(gamma=0.5)    = 32/3
kappa_0(gamma=0.1)    = 800/19 = 42.1053
kappa_0(gamma=0.01)   = 402.0101

lim_{gamma->0+} kappa_0(gamma) = oo

*** CENTRAL FINDING ***
kappa_0 is NOT a gamma-independent constant. The illustrative value
kappa_0=2.25 used by the Gap-1 front (Estagio 33) for concreteness is
neither the correct value at any single gamma (kappa_0(1)=8, not 2.25),
nor a valid stand-in for a gamma-independent constant, since the true
kappa_0(gamma) = 8/(gamma(2-gamma)) diverges as gamma -> 0+.

Done.
